========================================================================
WHY covering forces the jump rung1 -> rung14:
========================================================================
A DC family must contain 1 (and be 'complete' below its max). At base q, the
distance-1 lander is v ≡ ±a^{-1}. For the margin to exceed 1/14 the family must
place NO runner within distance q/14 of 0. Test: can a DC family beat 1/14 at a
base smaller than 183?  Scan minimal DC families {1..12, f}:

Smallest-M DC extension that beats 1/14: M=1/13=0.07692 at f=14, base 13  == 14/183 crux CONFIRMED as the floor.

MECHANISM SUMMARY: DC forces 1..12 in; to exceed 1/14 you must reach a base whose
distance-1 lander is a runner you DON'T have. The smallest such base for a DC set is
q=183 (=13*14+1), where the lander is v=13 (absent) and 1&182 both sit at distance 14.
